      "content": "that makes sense. so if i'm trying to hammer home the idea of \"modernization,\" how can i argue that these organized systems were actually superior to the indigenous political or social structures that existed before? \n\nlike, instead of just saying they were \"different,\" can i frame it as though the pre-colonial systems were too fractured or inefficient to handle the complexities of a globalized industrial era, and that the colonial imposition was almost a necessary intervention to bring order and \"rationality\" to the region? i want to show that without that external structure, these nations might have struggled much longer to achieve any kind of cohesive statehood.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
